      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so i just updated our A records for the main client site but it's still pointing to the old server on my end even though i cleared my local cache. why does it take so long for dns changes to actually show up everywhere?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "DNS changes don't propagate instantly because each server hosting the DNS records caches the data for a specific period known as the Time To Live (TTL). When you update an A record, your provider tells existing DNS servers the new IP, but they ignore it until their cache expires. This process typically takes anywhere from how long is set in your DNS settings to 24 hours globally. To speed things up, setting a lower TTL before making changes can minimize the delay window for future updates.",
